  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis surfaced while adapting Servo's module loading code to the new API provided by SpiderMonkey ESR 153, [upon rejection of loadingPromise](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#fetch-the-descendants-of-and-link-a-module-script), _moduleScript's error to rethrow_ will be set to the first error encountered during module loading which is stored inside _state.[[ErrorToRethrow]]_.\n\nIn particular step 7 of [HostLoadImportedModule](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#hostloadimportedmodule) will validate all the requested dependencies of a module; however this will not happen if the first _ModuleRequest record_ has an unsupported attribute, `InnerModuleLoading` will reject the promise instead of calling `HostLoadImportedModule`.\nTherefore _state.[[ErrorToRethrow]]_ will be left empty, and subsequent code will treat the failure as a network error, ignoring the `SyntaxError`.",
